      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T21:05:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeh. ServiceState works as a temporary state storage for ArfcnRsrpBoot info in original design. I think this is where all the confusing come from.\n\nThe ArfcnRsrpBoost info is maintained and updated (the set method ServiceState#setArfcnRsrpBoost) in SSC, but the info retrieval (get method ServiceState#getArfcnRsrpBoost) are used by both CellSignalStrengthLte and CellSignalStrengthNr.\n\nI think the info go through ServiceState because the current method accept ServiceState as the parameter(SignalStrength#updateLevel(PersistableBundle, ServiceState):\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/telephony/java/android/telephony/CellSignalStrengthLte.java;l\u003d256?q\u003dupdateLevel\n\nOf cause we can bypass ServiceState and directly pass the  ArfcnRsrpBoost from SSC to CellSignalStrengthXXX ( e.g. by adding the third parameter to SignalStrength#updateLevel). But ArfcnRsrpBoot only applies to LTE and NR and it seems not be worthy to update the common API.\n\nPls let me know if this makes sense to you.",
      "parentUuid": "1bef5cc4_a474a6ef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 715,
        "startChar": 9,
